gtsummary
Another popular packages is gt (stands for “great tables”) and its ‘add-on’, gtsummary. It has lots of customization (which can get overwhelming!) but fortunately the documentation is pretty good and there are plenty of code samples. View the documentation here
Example: get the mean differences table for political_scale, life_satisfaction, and financial_satisfaction, grouped by sex

library(gtsummary)

wvs_cleaned |&gt; 
    dplyr::select(life_satisfaction, financial_satisfaction, freedom_of_choice, sex) |&gt;
    tbl_summary(by = sex) |&gt;
    add_difference()

